/target
# The eBPF crate is a standalone workspace (excluded from the root) and builds
# into its own target dir.
/crates/bpf/target
**/*.rs.bk
/cordon-audit.toml
/cordon-audit.policy.toml
/cordond.service
# Claude Code. `settings.local.json` is per-machine (a personal permission
# allowlist); the un-suffixed `.claude/settings.json` is the shared one and stays
# trackable, like .vscode/settings.json. Worktrees are nested checkouts carrying
# their own .git and target/ — 1.5G at last look, and never committable.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/worktrees/
